<task id="011" project="spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2">
  <metadata>
    <title>EmailComposer MCP host (sibling of the Xrm host)</title>
    <phase>0 Removal, prerequisites and seams</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds .ts code to @spaarke/ui-components (shared library consumed by the Console); tags include react and frontend</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Sibling implementation of an existing injected interface with two canonical references to copy (createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts, useXrmEmailHostProps.ts)</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>A</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Adds new files beside EmailComposer and one export line in its index.ts; no other Group A task touches Spaarke.UI.Components</parallel-reason>
    <deps>none</deps>
    <tags>react, typescript, frontend, fluent-ui</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Add an MCP host for EmailComposer: a sibling of createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts / useXrmEmailHostProps.ts that implements the same injected host interface over an injectable tool-call transport (callTool(name, args)), so task 040's widget can compose and send through app-only MCP tools without Xrm. Keep the transport an injected interface; the real MCP transport is task 021's.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Follow ADRs strictly. Expert in React host-prop injection and the EmailComposer engine.</role>
  <goal>createMcpEmailComposeHandlers / useMcpEmailHostProps exist beside the Xrm versions, implement the same host contract using a McpToolCaller interface, are unit-tested with a fake caller, and leave the Xrm host and every existing EmailComposer test unchanged.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-12 / FR-16 ("Email compose: EmailComposer, with an MCP host in place of createXrmEmailComposeHandlers / useXrmEmailHostProps"). Reuse scan row "Email compose component": host injected; Xrm handlers in createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts / useXrmEmailHostProps.ts; EmailRecipients.tsx:110 is display-only. v1 email scope (owner): To/Cc, subject, rich body, regarding a matter (required), attachments chosen from that matter's Spaarke documents, archived to the matter. Tool names the host calls (fixed here, implemented in Phase 2–3): spaarke_list_documents (023) for the attachment picker, spaarke_send_email (040, app-only) for Send.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/createMcpEmailComposeHandlers.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/useMcpEmailHostProps.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/mcpToolCaller.ts (type McpToolCaller = { callTool(name: string, args: Record&lt;string, unknown&gt;): Promise&lt;McpToolCallResult&gt; } and the result shape: structuredContent, isError, reasonCode)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/index.ts (export the three)</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/__tests__/createMcpEmailComposeHandlers.test.ts</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/__tests__/useMcpEmailHostProps.test.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/useXrmEmailHostProps.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/EmailComposer.types.ts</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies/>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">The MCP host lives in the existing EmailComposer folder of @spaarke/ui-components; it imports no @modelcontextprotocol/* package (McpToolCaller is a local structural type) and no Xrm global.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The MCP host implements the same host-prop contract as useXrmEmailHostProps for the v1 scope only: recipients To/Cc typed entry, subject, rich body, regarding matter (required, pre-set by the host, not user-picked), attachments from the regarding matter's documents (via spaarke_list_documents), Send (via spaarke_send_email with an idempotency key generated once per compose session and reused on retry). Callbacks outside v1 (record lookup dialogs, templates, AI draft, local upload, relationships) are left undefined so the engine hides them.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">A tool result with isError maps to the composer's existing send-failure path (describeSendFailure) with the tool's reasonCode; nothing is retried automatically except by the user pressing Send again with the same idempotency key.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">The Xrm host files and every existing test under EmailComposer/__tests__/ are unchanged and pass.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Run npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund if needed; run the package's jest suite.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/constraints/pcf.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/control-initialization.md</file>
      <file>.claude/patterns/pcf/theme-management.md</file>
      <file>src/client/pcf/CLAUDE.md</file>
      <file>docs/guides/PCF-DEPLOYMENT-GUIDE.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/ui-test/SKILL.md</file>
      <file>.claude/skills/fluent-v9-component/SKILL.md</file>
