      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-012-shared-components.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-021-fluent-design-system.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-045-communication-architecture.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/reuse-scan.md</file>
      <file>projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/spec.md</file>
    </files>
    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Xrm email host" location="src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/useXrmEmailHostProps.ts">The host-prop shape to mirror; swap Xrm calls for callTool</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read useXrmEmailHostProps and createXrmEmailComposeHandlers; list which host props are v1 and which are left undefined, in the task notes.</step>
    <step order="2">Write mcpToolCaller.ts, createMcpEmailComposeHandlers.ts and useMcpEmailHostProps.ts; export them.</step>
    <step order="3">Write the two test files with a fake McpToolCaller; run the EmailComposer jest suite.</step>
    <step order="4">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]` (the bracketed ASCII token is mandatory, the emoji alone is not greppable: task-create Step 5, FAILURE-MODES G-16), set the POML &lt;status&gt; to completed, and run pwsh scripts/check-task-status-drift.ps1</step>
    <step order="5">If any deviations from plan, document in projects/spaarkeai-mcp-bff-api-r2/notes/ (decisions go to notes/decisions.md)</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the engine cannot hide an out-of-scope callback when it is undefined (it renders a broken control instead), STOP and escalate rather than changing EmailComposer.tsx's contract.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>notes/reuse-scan.md row "Email compose component": EmailComposer.tsx host injected; Xrm handlers createXrmEmailComposeHandlers.ts / useXrmEmailHostProps.ts; verdict "Extend: add an MCP host implementation". CAPABILITY-INDEX row 12 (communication core) on the server side.</existing>
    <extension>Yes: a sibling implementation of the existing injected host interface; the engine is not changed.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The Copilot compose widget (task 040) cannot attach matter documents or send without Xrm, so FR-12's widget send path fails.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Composer renders with MCP host (harness)">
      <steps>
        <step>Mount EmailComposer with useMcpEmailHostProps and a fake caller in the jest/RTL harness</step>
        <step>Verify To, Cc, subject, body and the matter-documents attachment picker render; template, AI draft and local upload controls do not</step>
        <step>Check for console errors</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>v1 controls only, no console errors</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Dark Mode Compliance (ADR-021)">
      <steps>
        <step>Render the harness under the Fluent dark theme</step>
        <step>Verify backgrounds and text use semantic tokens</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>No hard-coded colours</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="npm">jest in src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/createMcpEmailComposeHandlers.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/useMcpEmailHostProps.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/mcpToolCaller.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/__tests__/createMcpEmailComposeHandlers.test.ts</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/EmailComposer/__tests__/useMcpEmailHostProps.test.ts</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Send calls callTool("spaarke_send_email", …) once with To, Cc, subject, body, regarding matter id, selected document ids and an idempotency key; a second Send after a failure reuses the same key.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The attachment picker lists documents from callTool("spaarke_list_documents", { regarding matter }) only.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an isError result with a reasonCode surfaces through the existing send-failure path with that code; no automatic retry happens.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the MCP host never reads window.Xrm or calls getXrm (spied in tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every existing EmailComposer test passes unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named in these criteria; anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in the task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-12, FR-16. Task 021's shared transport must satisfy McpToolCaller; task 040 wires them.</notes>

